    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py` and wrote 11 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. All 11 pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nThe function validates `start`, `n` and the holidays, raising `TypeError` as the spec says. It then steps one day at a time in the right direction, counting only weekdays that aren't holidays. For `n == 0` it returns `start`, or the next business day if `start` isn't one. The tests cover forward and backward moves, weekends, `n == 0`, holidays (including weekend holidays and generators) and the `TypeError` cases.\n\nThe command output only shows pass/fail. I haven't seen coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit results, so I can't say whether those gates will pass. The function is small and the tests exercise all its branches, so I expect them to.",
